<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Why Fitting Scaling Laws Separately?</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We justify our decision to fit two separate scaling laws—one for models trained from scratch and another for bootstrapped pretraining—instead of employing a unified formulation that spans all stages.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">First, the scaling behavior of models trained from scratch is expected to differ from that of models undergoing bootstrapping.
Specifically, at the limit <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{1}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{1}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, grown models are initialized from a pretrained base model, whereas scratch-trained models start from random weights.
This difference in initialization leads to distinct learning dynamics and, consequently, different scaling law parameters.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly, the scaling behavior of the base model differs from that of the second-stage training in the limit <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{2}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{2}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>. As shown in Figure <a href="#A3.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ C.5 Model Growth Details ‣ Appendix C Training Details ‣ From Acceleration to Saturation: Scaling Behavior of Bootstrapped Language Model Pretraining" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, second-stage training often begins with a <em id="A4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">rewarming</em> phase, during which the loss initially increases before decreasing.
This early instability deviates from the expected scaling of dense models, although the overall trend remains correlated—supporting the validity of Condition 1, due to function preservation and empirical observations that rewarming does not entirely disrupt loss behavior (as quoted from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>: “In practice, few empirical phenomena obey power laws for all values of <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>”).</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, our preliminary experiments indicate that a unified scaling law does not provide a satisfactory fit across both stages.
We therefore opt to model them separately.
We also note that there may exist alternative functional forms that could better capture the full range of behavior, but they may violate some of the well-established conditions for scaling laws (power law), and may overcomplicate the analysis or overfit the data; hence, we leave their exploration to future work.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>More Practical Implications</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To further examine the trade-off between training from scratch and bootstrapped pretraining, we fit Chinchilla-style scaling laws to models trained <em id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">from scratch</em> on the same datasets used in our second-stage experiments, namely, code or math data for CPT, and the original dataset for model growth. In Figure <a href="#A5.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ Appendix E More Practical Implications ‣ From Acceleration to Saturation: Scaling Behavior of Bootstrapped Language Model Pretraining" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> and <a href="#A5.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ Appendix E More Practical Implications ‣ From Acceleration to Saturation: Scaling Behavior of Bootstrapped Language Model Pretraining" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>, we plot the validation loss as a function of training tokens for both approaches, across a range of sunk costs, using a fixed model size of 7B. For CPT on code data, we find that models trained from scratch begin to outperform bootstrapped models (pretrained on 10T tokens) once more than 300B tokens of domain-specific data are used.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F10" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.06548v1/stack_sunk_cost.png" id="A5.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/218;" width="286" height="218" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 10</span>: </span><span id="A5.F10.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
<span id="A5.F10.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Tokens required for from-scratch training to catch up with bootstrapped pretraining.</span>
We compare loss-versus-token plots of from-scratch and bootstrapped pretraining at various base model training budgets (sunk costs).
Stacking is only considered efficient when <math id="A5.F10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\rm scratch}&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>scratch</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\rm scratch}&lt;</annotation></semantics></math> sunk cost. We observe that the efficiency of stacking diminishes with sunk cost. </span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A5.F11" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.06548v1/cpt_sunk_cost.png" id="A5.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/221;" width="286" height="221" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 11</span>: </span><span id="A5.F11.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
<span id="A5.F11.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Tokens required for from-scratch training to catch up with bootstrapped pretraining.</span>
Conclusion similar to those made in Figure <a href="#A5.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ Appendix E More Practical Implications ‣ From Acceleration to Saturation: Scaling Behavior of Bootstrapped Language Model Pretraining" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> can be made for CPT on code data, where the scaling efficiency decreases with first-stage training tokens.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Compute Optimality of Model Growth</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For model growth with growth factor 2, we want to scale <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{2},D_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{2},D_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> optimally, <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N^{\rm opt}_{2},D^{\rm opt}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>opt</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>opt</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N^{\rm opt}_{2},D^{\rm opt}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, given a FLOPs budget and fixing <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, while minimizing the loss <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, which we write as <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{D_{1}}(D_{2},N_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{D_{1}}(D_{2},N_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Here, <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the model size before growth, and <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{2}=2N_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{2}=2N_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This is equivalent to solving the following:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left.\frac{\partial}{\partial D_{2}}L_{D_{1}}(D_{2},C_{2}/12D_{2})\right|_{D_{2}=D_{2}^{\rm opt}}=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>opt</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left.\frac{\partial}{\partial D_{2}}L_{D_{1}}(D_{2},C_{2}/12D_{2})\right|_{D_{2}=D_{2}^{\rm opt}}=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left.\frac{\partial}{\partial N_{1}}L_{D_{1}}(C_{2}/12N_{1},N_{1})\right|_{N_{1}=N^{\rm opt}_{1}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>opt</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left.\frac{\partial}{\partial N_{1}}L_{D_{1}}(C_{2}/12N_{1},N_{1})\right|_{N_{1}=N^{\rm opt}_{1}}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where we have used <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{2}=2N_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{2}=2N_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}=6N_{2}D_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}=6N_{2}D_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Solving the above equations leads to</p>
<table id="A5.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D^{\rm opt}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>opt</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D^{\rm opt}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=G\left(\frac{C_{2}}{12}\right)^{a}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=G\left(\frac{C_{2}}{12}\right)^{a},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle N^{\rm opt}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>opt</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle N^{\rm opt}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=G^{-1}\left(\frac{C_{2}}{12}\right)^{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=G^{-1}\left(\frac{C_{2}}{12}\right)^{b}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A5.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneq\left(\frac{A_{\rm eff}\alpha_{\rm eff}}{B\beta}\right)^{1/(\alpha_{\rm eff}+\beta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneq\left(\frac{A_{\rm eff}\alpha_{\rm eff}}{B\beta}\right)^{1/(\alpha_{\rm eff}+\beta)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneq\frac{\beta}{\alpha_{\rm eff}+\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneq\frac{\beta}{\alpha_{\rm eff}+\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneq\frac{\alpha_{\rm eff}}{\alpha_{\rm eff}+\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneq\frac{\alpha_{\rm eff}}{\alpha_{\rm eff}+\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{\rm eff}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{\rm eff}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneq AD_{1}^{-\alpha_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneq AD_{1}^{-\alpha_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha_{\rm eff}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha_{\rm eff}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneq\alpha_{2}-\alpha_{3}\log D_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneq\alpha_{2}-\alpha_{3}\log D_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">We can henceforth relate <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\rm opt}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>opt</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\rm opt}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N^{\rm opt}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>opt</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N^{\rm opt}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> via</p>
<table id="A5.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\rm opt}_{2}=G\left(GN^{\rm opt}_{1}\right)^{a/b}\propto\left(N^{\rm opt}_{1}\right)^{\beta/\alpha_{2}-\alpha_{3}\log D_{1}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>opt</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>opt</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∝</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>opt</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\rm opt}_{2}=G\left(GN^{\rm opt}_{1}\right)^{a/b}\propto\left(N^{\rm opt}_{1}\right)^{\beta/\alpha_{2}-\alpha_{3}\log D_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A5.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N^{\rm opt}_{1}=G^{-1}\left(G^{-1}D^{\rm opt}_{2}\right)^{b/a}\propto\left(D^{\rm opt}_{2}\right)^{(\alpha_{2}-\alpha_{3}\log D_{1})/\beta}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>opt</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>opt</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∝</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>opt</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N^{\rm opt}_{1}=G^{-1}\left(G^{-1}D^{\rm opt}_{2}\right)^{b/a}\propto\left(D^{\rm opt}_{2}\right)^{(\alpha_{2}-\alpha_{3}\log D_{1})/\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
